==Strategy==
It's imperative that you start off slow and pick off each Owlbrow before you start the boss wave, as the Owlbrows will shred anything that tries to get a hit on Gorilliam. It is best to use a unit like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] for this due to its [[Money Up]] ability and high burst damage, but after the 2nd Stage, you'll need to pair it with something else like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]]. For the Zombies, it's best to not be actively deploying something with [[Zombie Killer|Z-Killer]], but rather something with [[Soulstrike]] like [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Chief]] only when there is a corpse that concerns you. You need as much space in the Deploy Limit to deal with Gorilliam. It's also possible your units might brute force the zombies to the point where they won't be a problem at all, removing the need for an Anti-Zombie in the first place.

